  📗
    Adds middleware to the pipeline. Runs in registration order. A layer that
    raises is answered for like a handler that raises, and the layers outside
    it are handed that answer: the rest of the pipeline never raises.
  📗
  ❗️ 🧱 layer 🍇📨🍇📨➡️📬🍉➡️📬🚧🚧🍉 🍇
    🐻 layers layer❗️
  🍉

  📗
    Adds an error mapper. When a handler or a layer of middleware raises, the
    mappers are asked about the error in the order they were added, and the
    first response one of them gives is the answer. A mapper knows its errors
    by casting, ↪️ 🔲 error 🚧🔸📭 ➡️ missing 🍇, and gives no value for the
    rest. The cast must be bound to a variable like that: one that fails and
    was handed straight to a call frees the error. When none answers, an error
    that carries a problem is answered with that problem, and any other with
    a 500.
  📗
  ❗️ 🚑 mapper 🍇🚧 📨➡️🍬📬🍉 🍇
    🚑 rescue mapper❗️
