  📗
    The app's own tokens, made as its settings say: signed with
    auth.tokenKey, from auth.issuer and for auth.audience when those are set,
    lasting auth.tokenSeconds, with auth.leewaySeconds between two clocks.
    Call it once the settings are loaded, and keep what it gives.

    Without a key the app takes 32 random bytes from the system and says so
    in its log, as a warning: tokens signed with them end with this run, and
    no other server takes them. The key itself is never logged.
