  📗
    Registers a health endpoint, GET *path*, and returns the route. A probe
    is answered 200 with {"status":"ok"}; 503 with "failing" when one of
    the checks added with 💓 app name check❗️ does not pass, each check
    listed; and 503 with "stopping" once the server has been asked to stop,
    so that whoever sends the requests can take the server out before it is
    gone. With server.shutdownDelayMs set, the server goes on answering for
    that long after it was asked to stop, and this is how a load balancer
    learns of it meanwhile.
  📗
